    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but \"cognitive biases\" feels like such a convenient way to brush it under the rug. if it's just \"attentional cues,\" why is the pattern so consistent across totally different industries? it's like they're all using the same manual. \n\nif you look at \"unleash your potential,\" it's not just a suggestion, it's a command that bypasses the logical part of the brain and targets the ego directly. can you actually map out the linguistic mechanics of how these specific word choices bypass the analytical mind? like, what's the actual neurological or psychological 'loop' they're closing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
